{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"We will solve this by integrating by parts. We know that \n\n$\\qquad\\displaystyle\\int u(x)v\\,^\\prime(x)dx = u(x)v(x)-\\int u\\,^\\prime(x)v(x)dx\\,$.\n\nWe can rewrite this as\n\n$\\qquad\\displaystyle\\int u\\ dv = uv-\\int v\\ du\\,$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In this problem we will let $~u = x~$ and $~dv=\\sin(2x)\\, dx\\,$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Then $~du = dx~$ and $~v = \\displaystyle\\int \\sin(2x)\\,dx = -\\dfrac{\\cos(2x)}{2}\\,$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Integration by parts gives\n\n$\\displaystyle\\qquad\\int^\\pi_0x\\sin(2x)\\,dx = x\\cdot\\Big(-\\dfrac{\\cos(2x)}{2}\\Big)\\Bigg]_0^\\pi-\\int^\\pi_0-\\dfrac{\\cos(2x)}{2}dx$\n\n$\\displaystyle\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad~~=  -\\dfrac{x\\cos(2x)}{2}+\\bigg(\\dfrac{\\sin(2x)}4\\bigg)\\Bigg]^\\pi_0$\n\n$\\displaystyle\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad~~=\\Bigg(-\\dfrac{\\pi\\,\\cos(2\\pi)}{2}+\\dfrac{\\sin(2\\pi)}{4}\\Bigg)$\n\n$\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad-\\Bigg(-\\dfrac{\\pi \\cdot\\,\\cos\\,0}{2}+\\dfrac{\\sin\\,0}{4}\\Bigg)$\n\n$\\displaystyle\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad~~=-\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}+0 = -\\dfrac{\\pi}2$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Evaluate $~~\\displaystyle\\int^\\pi_0x\\sin(2x) dx\\,$.\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$\\dfrac{\\pi}2$","correct":false},{"content":"$-\\dfrac{\\pi}2$","correct":true},{"content":"$0$","correct":false},{"content":"$-\\pi$","correct":false},{"content":"$-\\dfrac{\\pi}3$","correct":false}],"countChoices":false,"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major